                <h2>Professional Interlock Installation - The Smart Backup Power Solution</h2>
                <p>An interlock kit transforms your portable generator into a safe, code-compliant whole-house backup power system. For a fraction of the cost of automatic standby generators, you get reliable backup power that can run all the lights and outlets in your home.</p>

                <p>This isn't a DIY extension cord solution. It's a professional, permanent installation that safely connects your generator to your electrical panel, allowing you to power any circuit in your home during an outage.</p>

                <h2>How Generator Interlock Kits Work</h2>
                <p>An interlock kit is a mechanical device that ensures your main breaker and generator breaker cannot be on simultaneously. This prevents dangerous backfeeding that could injure utility workers or damage equipment.</p>

                <h3>The System Components</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Interlock plate:</strong> Mechanical sliding plate installed on your panel cover</li>
                    <li><strong>Generator inlet box:</strong> Weatherproof 30 or 50-amp connection mounted outside</li>
                    <li><strong>Generator breaker:</strong> New breaker in your panel for generator input</li>
                    <li><strong>Heavy wiring:</strong> 6 or 8 AWG copper from inlet to panel</li>
                    <li><strong>Connection cable:</strong> 50-amp cord from generator to inlet (sold separately)</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Step-by-Step Operation During Power Outage</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Verify outage:</strong> Check neighbors to confirm utility outage</li>
                    <li><strong>Position generator:</strong> Roll out to safe location (20+ feet from house)</li>
                    <li><strong>Start generator:</strong> Let warm up for 2-3 minutes</li>
                    <li><strong>Connect cable:</strong> Plug into generator and inlet box</li>
                    <li><strong>Turn off main breaker:</strong> Disconnects from utility</li>
                    <li><strong>Slide interlock plate:</strong> Allows generator breaker to turn on</li>
                    <li><strong>Turn on generator breaker:</strong> Powers your panel</li>
                    <li><strong>Manage circuits:</strong> Turn on breakers for needed circuits</li>
                </ol>

                <h2>Tri-Fuel Generators We Recommend and Supply</h2>

                <div class="surface-panel">
                    <h3>50-Amp Tri-Fuel Generators We Supply</h3>
                    <p>We supply and recommend tri-fuel generators that operate on gasoline, propane, or natural gas:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Power output:</strong> 9,500-12,000 starting watts</li>
                        <li><strong>50-amp capability:</strong> Powers all lights and standard outlets</li>
                        <li><strong>Electric start:</strong> Key fob remote starting</li>
                        <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> 8-12 hours on gasoline, unlimited on natural gas</li>
                        <li><strong>Noise level:</strong> 72-74 dB at 23 feet</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4>Natural Gas Connection Option</h4>
                    <p>We coordinate with licensed gas contractors to install quick-disconnect fittings for natural gas operation. This eliminates refueling during extended outages - your generator runs as long as the gas flows. Contact for details.</p>
                </div>

                <h2>Using Your Existing Portable Generator</h2>
                <p>Already own a portable generator? We can install an interlock kit for it if it meets these requirements:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Minimum 30-amp output (7,500 watts)</li>
                    <li>L14-30 or L14-50 outlet</li>
                    <li>Floating neutral or bonded neutral compatible</li>
                    <li>Good working condition</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Professional interlock installation for your existing generator.</strong> Contact for walkthrough.</p>

                <h2>What Can You Power?</h2>

                <h3>With 50-Amp Generator (Recommended)</h3>
                <div class="content-callout">
                    <h4>Run Simultaneously:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>All lights in the house</li>
                        <li>All standard 120V outlets</li>
                        <li>Refrigerator and freezer</li>
                        <li>Furnace or boiler</li>
                        <li>Sump pump</li>
                        <li>Internet and home office</li>
                        <li>Microwave</li>
                        <li>Multiple TVs</li>
                        <li>Garage door openers</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h3>Load Management Required</h3>
                <div class="content-callout">
                    <h4>Large Loads (One at a Time):</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Electric water heater (turn off other loads first)</li>
                        <li>Electric dryer (if essential)</li>
                        <li>Electric range (one or two burners)</li>
                        <li>Window AC units</li>
                        <li>Space heaters</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2>Installation Process - Same Day Service</h2>

                <h3>Morning: Assessment and Parts</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Evaluate your electrical panel</li>
                    <li>Confirm compatible interlock kit model</li>
                    <li>Determine inlet box location</li>
                    <li>Calculate wire run distance</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Afternoon: Installation</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Install weatherproof inlet box outside</li>
                    <li>Run wiring from inlet to panel (through wall/basement)</li>
                    <li>Install interlock plate on panel</li>
                    <li>Add dedicated generator breaker</li>
                    <li>Make all connections and torque to spec</li>
                    <li>Test mechanical interlock operation</li>
                    <li>Complete permit documentation</li>
                    <li>Train you on safe operation</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Safety and Code Compliance</h2>
                <p>DIY generator connections are illegal and dangerous. Our professional installation ensures:</p>

                <h3>Electrical Safety</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>No backfeeding to utility lines (protects linemen)</li>
                    <li>Proper grounding and bonding</li>
                    <li>Correct wire sizing for amperage</li>
                    <li>NEMA-rated components throughout</li>
                    <li>Torqued connections to manufacturer specs</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Code Compliance</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Meets NEC Article 702 requirements</li>
                    <li>Michigan Electrical Code compliant</li>
                    <li>Local permit and inspection</li>
                    <li>Insurance company acceptable</li>
                    <li>Documented installation for home sale</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Maintenance and Operation Tips</h2>

                <h3>Generator Maintenance (DIY)</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Monthly:</strong> Start and run for 15 minutes under load</li>
                    <li><strong>Before each use:</strong> Check oil level</li>
                    <li><strong>Seasonal:</strong> Change oil (every 50 hours)</li>
                    <li><strong>Annual:</strong> Replace spark plug and air filter</li>
                    <li><strong>Fuel:</strong> Use stabilizer if storing over 30 days</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Operating Best Practices</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Keep written procedure posted near panel</li>
                    <li>Practice switchover quarterly</li>
                    <li>Monitor total load - don't exceed generator capacity</li>
                    <li>Start large loads one at a time</li>
                    <li>Keep spare oil and filters on hand</li>
                    <li>Store extra fuel safely (follow local codes)</li>
                </ul>

